{{!--
    Effects tab (#9): the ship's ActiveEffects, split into an active and an inactive list.

    Structurally identical to daggerheart's own
    `templates/sheets/actors/character/effects.hbs` - the same `.effects-sections` wrapper around
    two `inventory-items` fieldsets, the same "Active Effects"/"Inactive Effects" split, the same
    `isGlassy`/`canCreate` treatment, and the same `disabled=true` marker on the second one so its
    "+" creates an already-disabled effect. Only the partial names differ (module-owned copies, per
    docs/adr/0002-spaceship-sheet-independent-application.md) and `canCreate` is spelled
    `@root.editable` inside our fieldset partial rather than passed in, since every list on this
    sheet gates creation on the same flag.

    `isEffect=true` is what tells the shared row partial to render an ActiveEffect row - the
    enable/disable toggle instead of an equip toggle, and `data-type="effect"` for the context menu -
    mirroring the `type='effect'` branches in daggerheart's own `inventory-item-V2.hbs`. Everything
    else on the row is unchanged, because `DhActiveEffect` supplies the same `_getTags`/
    `hasDescription`/`toChat` an Item does.

    The `effects.actives`/`effects.inactives` context is built in
    `SpaceshipActorSheet#buildEffectsContext`, off the same `allApplicableEffects` source and the
    same `effect.active` split as daggerheart's `_prepareEffectsContext`.
--}}
<section class="tab {{tab.id}} {{tab.cssClass}} spaceship-effects" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}">
    <div class="effects-sections">
        {{> "dhscifi.inventory-items"
            title="DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Effects.Active"
            isGlassy=true
            isEffect=true
            collection=effects.actives
        }}

        {{> "dhscifi.inventory-items"
            title="DHSCIFI.Spaceship.Effects.Inactive"
            isGlassy=true
            isEffect=true
            createDisabled=true
            collection=effects.inactives
        }}
    </div>
</section>
